  "title": "Erdős Problem #44",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $N\\geq 1$ and $A\\subset \\{1,\\ldots,N\\}$ be a Sidon set. Is it true that, for any $\\epsilon>0$, there exist $M$ and $B\\subset \\{N+1,\\ldots,M\\}$ (which may depend on $N,A,\\epsilon$) such that $A\\cup B\\subset \\{1,\\ldots,M\\}$ is a Sidon set of size at least $(1-\\epsilon)M^{1/2}$?",
